Name: MOLE cryptographic and protocol stack (mole-p256, ec-ihat, ec-act, mole-core)
Short Name: mole
URL: https://github.com/Moderation-of-unLinkable-Endorsements/mole-p256-rs
URL: https://github.com/Moderation-of-unLinkable-Endorsements/internet-drafts
Version: draft-ladd-mole-ec-ihat-00, draft-schlesinger-mole-ec-act-00, draft-jms-mole-protocols-01, draft-jms-mole-http-transport-01
License: Apache-2.0, MIT
License File: LICENSE-APACHE, LICENSE-MIT
Security Critical: no
Shipped: no

Description:
The cryptographic and wire/HTTP transport implementations for the MOLE
(Moderation of unLinkable Endorsements) browser prototype:

  * mole_p256: shared P-256 group, constant-time scalar/field arithmetic,
    RFC 9380 hash-to-curve/scalar, key/nonce derivations, and zeroization
    primitives over Chromium's in-tree BoringSSL (`bssl_sys`).
  * ec_ihat: EC-IHAT (`EC-IHATv1-P256-SHA256`, endorsement type 0x0002) per
    draft-ladd-mole-ec-ihat-00.
  * ec_act: EC-ACT (`EC-ACTv1-P256-SHA256`, credential type 0x0001, base-2
    balances in `[0, 2^L)`) per draft-schlesinger-mole-ec-act-00.
  * mole-core: wire codecs, `Mole` HTTP authentication scheme (`WWW-Authenticate`,
    `Authorization`, `Mole-Credential`), recovery/signoff handles, and JSON
    configuration schemas per draft-jms-mole-protocols-01 and
    draft-jms-mole-http-transport-01.

Local Modifications:
  * Confines BoringSSL `bssl_sys` FFI to `mole_p256` with constant-time
    uncompressed point table selection (`Point::ct_select`), constant-time
    scalar `PartialEq`, and redacted `Scalar` `Debug`.
  * Includes self-contained `#![no_std]` volatile zeroization (`mole_p256::zeroize`)
    and FIPS 202 SHAKE128 (`ec_act::shake128`) so no custom BoringSSL C++ shims
    or extra `//third_party/rust` crates are required.

Experimental prototype code gated behind the `ModeratedEndorsements` feature.
